1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,587
See these two pieces?

2
00:00:01,887 --> 00:00:02,556
Watch.

3
00:00:04,633 --> 00:00:07,062
Three moves, and that pair is home.

4
00:00:07,333 --> 00:00:11,696
By the end of this video, you'll solve every F2L pair like that.

5
00:00:11,996 --> 00:00:13,370
No memorising.

6
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:15,136
Just three animals.

7
00:00:15,733 --> 00:00:18,401
This is the F2L hunting story.

8
00:00:18,701 --> 00:00:21,196
Grab your cube, and let's get into it.

9
00:00:21,767 --> 00:00:23,463
Quick refresher first.

10
00:00:23,763 --> 00:00:26,315
F2L means first two layers.

11
00:00:26,615 --> 00:00:29,530
You've already got your white cross on the bottom.

12
00:00:29,933 --> 00:00:32,964
Now we pair up a corner with its matching edge...

13
00:00:33,367 --> 00:00:35,633
and drop that pair into its slot.

14
00:00:36,033 --> 00:00:39,344
Do that four times, and the first two layers are done.

15
00:00:39,767 --> 00:00:42,569
To make this stick, we'll tell it as a story.

16
00:00:42,869 --> 00:00:44,985
The white corner is our hunter.

17
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:48,507
The edge with the same two colours is its prey.

18
00:00:48,933 --> 00:00:52,619
And the empty slot down here? That's its den. Its home.

19
00:00:53,033 --> 00:00:56,893
When the hunter catches its prey, they join up. That's a kill.

20
00:00:57,193 --> 00:00:59,368
Then it carries the prey home.

21
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,099
Three quick rules, and you're ready.

22
00:01:02,399 --> 00:01:05,895
One. The top layer is free. Turn it as much as you like.

23
00:01:06,267 --> 00:01:09,656
Two. A side face only turns a quarter turn out...

24
00:01:09,956 --> 00:01:11,643
and then comes straight back.

25
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:14,002
And three, the golden rule.

26
00:01:14,302 --> 00:01:17,868
When a side face turns, a slot comes up to the top.

27
00:01:18,168 --> 00:01:22,303
Make sure it's the empty den... never a slot you've already solved.

28
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:24,790
So which hunter have you got?

29
00:01:25,090 --> 00:01:27,818
Look at the top colours of the two pieces.

30
00:01:28,118 --> 00:01:31,359
Different colours, like a tiger's stripes? Tiger.

31
00:01:31,833 --> 00:01:34,585
The same colour on both? Crocodile.

32
00:01:35,067 --> 00:01:38,202
And if the white sticker points at the sky... eagle.

33
00:01:38,502 --> 00:01:40,161
That's it. Three hunters.

34
00:01:40,633 --> 00:01:42,716
Let's start with the easiest one.

35
00:01:43,016 --> 00:01:46,487
Look at the top. Red on the hunter... green on the prey.

36
00:01:46,787 --> 00:01:49,265
Different colours. So, it's a tiger.

37
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:54,520
A tiger always hunts from its den. It's sitting right above the empty slot...

38
00:01:54,933 --> 00:01:57,690
and its prey is waiting just behind it.

39
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,537
Want to follow along?

40
00:01:59,837 --> 00:02:06,506
Hold green in front, yellow on top, and do the scramble at the top of the screen. Pause if you need to.

41
00:02:06,933 --> 00:02:08,234
Okay, watch.

42
00:02:08,534 --> 00:02:11,302
The tiger jumps onto its prey. R.

43
00:02:11,633 --> 00:02:13,990
Drags it back over the den. U.

44
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:16,552
And takes it home. R prime.

45
00:02:16,867 --> 00:02:18,203
Why does that work?

46
00:02:18,503 --> 00:02:20,822
R swings the hunter to the back...

47
00:02:21,233 --> 00:02:23,283
right where the prey is waiting.

48
00:02:23,584 --> 00:02:26,446
That's why the prey has to be behind it.

49
00:02:26,867 --> 00:02:28,976
One more time, full speed.

50
00:02:29,267 --> 00:02:30,994
Three moves. That's it!

51
00:02:31,967 --> 00:02:34,266
Here's the same tiger, mirrored.

52
00:02:34,566 --> 00:02:37,510
Different colours on top, so it's still a tiger.

53
00:02:37,933 --> 00:02:40,689
But now its white sticker faces the front...

54
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:43,679
so its prey waits over on the left.

55
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:46,938
It jumps with the front face. F prime.

56
00:02:47,267 --> 00:02:49,244
Drags it back. U prime.

57
00:02:49,567 --> 00:02:50,918
And home. F.

58
00:02:51,233 --> 00:02:52,365
See the pattern?

59
00:02:52,665 --> 00:02:56,903
Every R becomes F prime, and the U turns go the other way.

60
00:02:57,333 --> 00:03:00,719
So learn one side, and you get the other one for free.

61
00:03:01,133 --> 00:03:02,394
Now, this one.

62
00:03:02,694 --> 00:03:06,530
Green on top of the hunter... and green on top of the prey.

63
00:03:06,830 --> 00:03:09,024
Same colour. That's a crocodile.

64
00:03:09,433 --> 00:03:11,578
And crocodiles don't chase.

65
00:03:11,878 --> 00:03:15,688
They hide under the water... and wait for the prey to come to them.

66
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:20,634
First, spin the top so its white sticker faces the right. U prime.

67
00:03:20,967 --> 00:03:22,765
Now it dives. R.

68
00:03:23,065 --> 00:03:26,777
And look, the empty den came up. So nothing gets broken.

69
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:30,686
The prey walks right over the hidden crocodile. U.

70
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,927
And... snap! R prime.

71
00:03:33,233 --> 00:03:34,932
Now, let's take it home.

72
00:03:35,232 --> 00:03:38,098
Swing the pair away from the den. U two.

73
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:40,095
Open the den, R.

74
00:03:40,395 --> 00:03:42,258
Slide it in, U prime.

75
00:03:42,558 --> 00:03:44,451
And close it, R prime.

76
00:03:44,767 --> 00:03:46,462
Here's the big idea.

77
00:03:46,762 --> 00:03:50,225
While the crocodile is hidden, turning the top can't touch it.

78
00:03:50,633 --> 00:03:55,565
So you move the prey right where you want it... then bring the hunter back up beside it.

79
00:03:55,967 --> 00:03:58,859
Full speed. Hide, wait, strike, and home.

80
00:04:00,233 --> 00:04:03,634
Red on top, and red on top. Crocodile again.

81
00:04:04,067 --> 00:04:08,971
This time we spin its white sticker to the front... so it dives through the front door.

82
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:10,701
Spin it. U.

83
00:04:11,033 --> 00:04:12,600
Dive. F prime.

84
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:15,265
The prey walks over. U prime.

85
00:04:15,567 --> 00:04:16,778
Snap! F.

86
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:18,993
Swing it away. U two.

87
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,853
Open, F prime.

88
00:04:21,153 --> 00:04:22,523
Slide in, U.

89
00:04:22,823 --> 00:04:23,960
Close, F.

90
00:04:24,267 --> 00:04:26,302
Same story, just mirrored.

91
00:04:26,602 --> 00:04:30,074
If you got the first crocodile, you've already got this one.

92
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,690
Last hunter.

93
00:04:31,990 --> 00:04:36,274
The white sticker is pointing straight up at the sky. That's an eagle.

94
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:38,398
Eagles hunt from the air.

95
00:04:38,698 --> 00:04:41,963
So first, the prey has to come down to the ground.

96
00:04:42,367 --> 00:04:44,966
Look at the prey's side colour. It's red.

97
00:04:45,266 --> 00:04:48,379
So line it up over the red centre. U.

98
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:50,662
Its top colour is green.

99
00:04:50,962 --> 00:04:54,156
So turn the red side away from green. R.

100
00:04:54,456 --> 00:04:55,628
Down it goes.

101
00:04:55,933 --> 00:04:58,604
Now the eagle flies over. U two.

102
00:04:58,933 --> 00:05:00,860
And grabs it! R prime.

103
00:05:01,167 --> 00:05:02,884
Swing it away. U.

104
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,630
And home. R, U prime, R prime.

105
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:07,628
Why away from green?

106
00:05:07,928 --> 00:05:11,902
Turning the other way would lift a slot you've already solved.

107
00:05:12,333 --> 00:05:15,645
Full speed. Line up, drop, fly, grab, home.

108
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:21,680
Okay. Sometimes a piece is stuck in the den, or the two pieces are stuck together.

109
00:05:21,980 --> 00:05:23,048
No problem.

110
00:05:23,467 --> 00:05:24,615
Lift it out...

111
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:26,211
step it clear...

112
00:05:26,633 --> 00:05:28,094
and put the face back.

113
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:29,912
And here's the trick.

114
00:05:30,212 --> 00:05:34,503
Lift it so it comes up as a tiger, with its prey right behind it.

115
00:05:34,803 --> 00:05:36,951
Then you already know the finish.

116
00:05:37,367 --> 00:05:41,055
Here, the hunter's stuck in its den, twisted the wrong way.

117
00:05:41,467 --> 00:05:44,492
Lift it out with the front face. F prime.

118
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,424
Step it clear. U.

119
00:05:46,733 --> 00:05:48,568
Put the face back. F.

120
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:52,217
And look. A tiger, with its prey right behind.

121
00:05:52,517 --> 00:05:55,210
You know this one. R, U, R prime.

122
00:05:55,533 --> 00:06:00,701
Now the prey is stuck in the den, flipped the wrong way. The hunter's waiting at the back.

123
00:06:01,133 --> 00:06:03,386
Lift the prey out. F prime.

124
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:05,608
Move it clear. U two.

125
00:06:05,933 --> 00:06:07,768
Put the face back. F.

126
00:06:08,068 --> 00:06:09,252
Another tiger!

127
00:06:09,567 --> 00:06:11,519
Pounce. R, U, R prime.

128
00:06:12,467 --> 00:06:15,702
And here, they're touching... but joined the wrong way.

129
00:06:16,002 --> 00:06:17,750
So we split them up first.

130
00:06:18,167 --> 00:06:20,102
Hide the prey. F prime.

131
00:06:20,433 --> 00:06:22,536
Walk the hunter away. U.

132
00:06:22,867 --> 00:06:24,685
Bring the prey back. F.

133
00:06:24,985 --> 00:06:25,718
Split!

134
00:06:26,033 --> 00:06:28,693
Walk the tiger to its den. U two.

135
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:29,990
And pounce!

136
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:33,305
Notice something?

137
00:06:33,605 --> 00:06:37,975
Every lift raised the empty den. Golden rule, every time.

138
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,558
Let's recap.

139
00:06:39,858 --> 00:06:43,699
Different colours on top? Tiger. Jump, drag back, home.

140
00:06:44,067 --> 00:06:48,285
Same colours? Crocodile. Hide, let the prey walk over, strike.

141
00:06:48,667 --> 00:06:52,596
White on top? Eagle. Line up, drop, fly over, grab.

142
00:06:52,967 --> 00:06:56,212
And if anything's stuck, lift it out as a tiger.

143
00:06:56,512 --> 00:06:59,605
Golden rule: only ever lift the empty den.

144
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,366
Don't worry if it feels slow at first.

145
00:07:02,666 --> 00:07:05,634
Everybody's F2L is slow at first.

146
00:07:06,067 --> 00:07:10,600
Say the story out loud while you turn... and the speed comes on its own.

147
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,670
Which hunter gave you the most trouble? Let me know in the comments.

148
00:07:14,970 --> 00:07:16,128
Happy hunting!

